# [Create embeddings]($heading.id('embeddings'))

`POST /v1/embeddings` maps input text to a numeric vector using the loaded
embedding checkpoint. Choose `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B` in the
[Embeddings catalog]($link.page('llmd/models').unsafeRef('embedding-checkpoints')).
The [quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').unsafeRef('send-an-embeddings-request'))
generates this request with the selected host port.

```sh
curl -sS --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/embeddings \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "input": "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.",
    "encoding_format": "float"
  }'
```

# [Request fields]($heading.id('embedding-request-fields'))

| Request field | Type and default | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `input` | String or array of strings, required | Send one nonempty string per vector. Token ID arrays are rejected. |
| `encoding_format` | String, `"float"` | Choose `"float"` for a JSON array of numbers or `"base64"` for encoded little-endian float32 bytes. |
| `dimensions` | Integer, model maximum | Sets the length of each vector. Qwen3-Embedding-8B supports 32 through 4,096 dimensions. |
| `model` | String, optional | May be omitted. LLMD embeds with the checkpoint loaded by the server. |

# [Read the response]($heading.id('embedding-response'))

`object` is `"list"` and `model` is the served
model ID. Each `data` entry has `object: "embedding"`, the zero-based input
`index`, and the vector in `embedding`. Entries follow input order.
`usage.prompt_tokens` and `usage.total_tokens` both count the tokens
embedded across all inputs. To inspect a float response, append
`| jq '.data[0].embedding | {dimensions: length, first_four: .[:4]}'` to
the command. See [Compare texts with embeddings]($link.page('llmd/text-similarity'))
for a client that ranks passages using the returned vectors.

# [Limits and errors]($heading.id('embedding-limits-and-errors'))

LLMD revision `fe922cff` accepts up to 2,048 strings
per request, up to 8,192 tokens per string, and up to 300,000 tokens in
total. Each tokenized string must also be shorter than the server's context
limit. An HTTP 400 response includes an `error.code`, such as
`model_not_supported` for a checkpoint without embedding support,
`invalid_dimensions` for a vector size outside the model's range, or
`too_many_tokens` for exceeding the endpoint's token limits.
A batch that LLMD cannot finish can return HTTP 503 with `resource_exhausted`.
